OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, A union leader has described as
OL,6, "outrageous" comments made by the
OL,7, employment minister about a pay rise
OL,8, this winter.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FMr Kenneth Clarke has said the current
OL,11,Flevel of inflation meant nobody needed
OL,12,Fa pay rise to maintain living
OL,13,Fstandards.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FBut Mr John Edmonds, of the General,
OL,16,FMunicipal, Boilermakers and Allied
OL,17,FTrades Union, said tax cuts were
OL,18,Fhelping high income earners, but the
OL,19,Fstandard of living for people on low
OL,20,Fpay was deteriorating.
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 14-09-86   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
