OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The American journalist, Mr Nicholas
OL,6, Daniloff, has been speaking about his
OL,7, two weeks' detention in Moscow.
OL,9,FMr Daniloff denied he had been under
OL,10,Finstructions from any US government
OL,11,Fagency, but would not discuss details
OL,12,Fof the charges of espionage brought
OL,13,Fagainst him by the Soviet Union.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FHe said there was no doubt he had been
OL,16,Fdetained as a result of the arrest in
OL,17,FNew York of Gennady Zakharov, who was
OL,18,Freleased from prison at the same time.
OL,19,F
OL,20,S/FA former CIA agent who defected to
OL,21,Fthe Soviet Union, Edward Lee Howard,
OL,22,Fhas appeared on Soviet TV to denounce
OL,23,FUS espionage activities.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18107
